<resources>
    <!-- Miracast (Wi-Fi Display) is not usable on this ROM, so keep it disabled.
         hardware/oplus' overlay (android.overlay.common, priority 200) sets it to true
         for ColorOS: there, system_server runs a Qualcomm-patched WifiDisplayController
         that binds com.qualcomm.wfd.service (WfdService.apk + wfdservice64 do ship on
         the device). Our build uses the AOSP/Lineage frameworks/base instead, where
         android.media.RemoteDisplay goes to
         MediaPlayerService::listenForRemoteDisplay, and AOSP removed that native
         implementation back in 2017 (d0a98fa05f "stagefright: remove Miracast sender
         code"), leaving only an ALOGE + return NULL. As a result RemoteDisplay.listen()
         throws IllegalStateException on the android.display thread and kills
         system_server (seen as a "SystemUI restart"/soft reboot) on every attempt to
         connect to a Miracast sink.
         Note: config_enableWifiDisplay is not in framework-res' overlayable list, so only
         an isStatic overlay like this one can change it (an RRO cannot).
         Flip this back to true once the Qualcomm WFD framework patch is ported. -->
    <bool name="config_enableWifiDisplay">false</bool>

    <!-- Whether a software navigation bar should be shown. NOTE: in the future this may be
         autodetected from the Configuration. -->
    <bool name="config_showNavigationBar">true</bool>

    <!-- Show the battery percentage by default; the user can still turn it off from
         Settings > Display (or Settings > Battery). -->
    <bool name="config_defaultBatteryPercentageSetting">true</bool>

    <!-- When true use the linux /dev/input/event subsystem to detect the switch changes
         on the headphone/microphone jack. When false use the older uevent framework. -->
    <bool name="config_useDevInputEventForAudioJack">true</bool>

